{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > make_read_obligation.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v2.json'))\nfor a in m['activities']:a.pop('behavior_ids',None)\nfor f in m['facts']:\n for k in ['established_by','consumed_by']:f.pop(k,None)\nm['behaviors'] += [dict(id='B_SINGLETON_TEST',primary_activity='A4',execution_owner='ProgressTracker.IsSingleton',protocol_context='Currently installed incoming/outgoing voter maps on the invoking raft instance',trigger='stepLeader evaluates singleton shortcut for MsgReadIndex',reads=['len(Voters[0])','len(Voters[1])'],implementation_guards=['Returns true exactly when incoming voter count is one and outgoing voter count is zero.'],produces_fact_ids=['F_SINGLETON_CARDINALITY'],source_ids=['S_TRACKER','S_SINGLETON_READ'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Supplies the predicate used to skip read quorum communication; it establishes cardinality only, not the invoking node membership.'}),dict(id='B_SINGLETON_READ',primary_activity='A1',execution_owner='raft.stepLeader / responseToReadIndexReq',protocol_context='StateLeader dispatch with a singleton installed voter configuration',trigger='MsgReadIndex from RawNode.ReadIndex',implementation_guards=['IsSingleton is checked before current-term committed-entry gating and without checking local Progress membership.'],consumes_fact_ids=['F_SINGLETON_CARDINALITY'],reads=['raftLog.committed','request From and context'],external_effects=['Directly append local ReadState for local requests or send MsgReadIndexResp for forwarded requests; no heartbeat quorum round in this branch.'],existing_protections=['StepDownOnRemoval=true changes removed leader to follower and prevents this leader branch.','Higher-term message also causes step-down, but the new singleton voter no longer sends replication messages to the removed node.'],source_ids=['S_SINGLETON_READ','S_READ_REPLY','S_READ_API','S_ACTIVATE','S_DISPATCH'],unknowns=['The emitted read-state endpoint is distinct from application-served read completion.'])]\nm['facts'].append(dict(id='F_SINGLETON_CARDINALITY',meaning='The installed configuration has exactly one incoming voter and no outgoing voters. This establishes no assertion that the querying raft instance is that voter.',identity={'owner':'invoking raft instance','configuration':'installed trk.Config voter maps'},validity_context='At IsSingleton evaluation; invalidated by configuration activation or configuration reconstruction.',representation=['ProgressTracker.IsSingleton() == true'],invalidators=['B_MEMBERSHIP','B_RECOVERY'],reinterpreters=[],durability='Derived from volatile installed configuration; persistence is through caller-managed configuration snapshots and applied entries.',recovery='ConfState reconstruction restores the maps whose lengths are queried.',source_ids=['S_TRACKER','S_ACTIVATE','S_INIT'],unknowns=[]))\nm['core_overview']['connection']['explanation']+=' The singleton read shortcut consumes only voter cardinality, whereas configuration activation may retain a removed leader role when StepDownOnRemoval is false. Therefore the local-voter identity needed for self-certification is a distinct relationship from retained role and singleton cardinality; StepDownOnRemoval provides an alternate protection.'\nm['core_overview']['connection']['behavior_ids']+=['B_SINGLETON_TEST','B_SINGLETON_READ']\nm['core_overview']['connection']['fact_ids'].append('F_SINGLETON_CARDINALITY')\nm['core_overview']['connection']['source_ids']+=['S_SINGLETON_READ','S_REMOVAL_OPTION']\nPath('read-map.json').write_text(json.dumps(m,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nq=dict(question='Does the singleton ReadOnlySafe shortcut use cardinality as if it also established that the responding instance is the sole voter after that instance applies its own removal?',importance='Self-certifying reads at an instance outside the active voter set lacks that configuration quorum support. Exploration showed an emitted index behind a completed successor write. This is a local read-certification concern; the documented application wait and caller retirement policy bound any claim of an externally served stale read.',disposition='ready_for_check',preferred_check='controlled_schedule',source_ids=[],participants=['Retained removed leader','Remaining singleton voter','RawNode caller'],objects=['Installed voter configuration','Unique-context ReadIndex request','Local ReadState'],contexts=['ReadOnlySafe','StepDownOnRemoval=false or true control','Committed/applied simple self-removal'],event_paths=['ProposeConfChange -> commit -> ApplyConfChange -> retained leader role -> ReadIndex -> IsSingleton -> ReadState'],activity_classes=['A1','A2'],behavior_ids=['B_SINGLETON_TEST','B_SINGLETON_READ','B_MEMBERSHIP','B_RECOVERY'],fact_ids=['F_SINGLETON_CARDINALITY'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B_CONTEXT':'Election and optional removal step-down determine dispatch role.','B_ENTRY':'RawNode caller owns serialized invocation and processing.','B_PROPOSE':'Actual old/new writes and removal entries establish legal history.','B_APPLY':'Caller activates configuration only while applying committed entries.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['StepDownOnRemoval=true prevents the leader shortcut after removal.','ReadIndex permits loss/pending and does not itself complete a user read; absence of ReadState is permitted.','Application must satisfy the returned index progress condition before serving reads.','External retirement of removed instances can prevent this invocation; no such automatic retirement exists in the selected RawNode entry.'],unknowns=['A client-visible stale read is not established: the exploration has local applied equal to the returned read index and does not satisfy a strict greater-than reading of the API wording.','An application that retires a removed RawNode avoids the selected invocation; deployment policy is outside the captured library.'],priority=3,trigger_rationale='Exploration 6127b12776d14d5f8a2557f7ecda3ef7 executed removal on both nodes, elected the remaining voter and applied its new write at index 6 before invoking a unique-context read on the removed instance. With step-down disabled, the removed instance returned ReadState index 4; with it enabled, no read state was emitted. The source singleton predicate checks counts, not local voter identity.')\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id'] in q['behavior_ids'] or b['id'] in q['supporting_behavior_ids']:q['source_ids']+=b['source_ids']\nq['source_ids']=list(dict.fromkeys(q['source_ids']+['S_TRACKER','S_ACTIVATE','S_INIT','S_READ_SAFE_EXPECTATION','S_SINGLETON_EXPECTATION','S_REMOVAL_OPTION']))\nclaim=dict(id='C_SINGLETON_READ_ELIGIBILITY',kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='When ReadOnlySafe certifies a read directly through the singleton shortcut without a quorum communication round for that request, the responding raft instance must itself be the sole configured voter. A pending or dropped request is permitted.',source_ids=['S_READ_SAFE_EXPECTATION','S_SINGLETON_EXPECTATION','S_READ_API'],scope=dict(description='Local RawNode ReadOnlySafe singleton self-certification after committed/applied simple membership change; live removed instances remain callable with StepDownOnRemoval disabled.',assumptions=['Serialized RawNode calls and contract-compliant persistence/application.','Unique request context and no earlier read or heartbeat acknowledgement associated with that context.','No caller policy retires the RawNode before the selected invocation.'],excluded=['Guarantee that every read request returns','External application read completion or client linearizability violation','Deployments which stop removed instances before invoking reads','Lease-based reads','Crash durability'],parameters={'ReadOnlyOption':'ReadOnlySafe','StepDownOnRemoval':False}),pending=[],grounding=dict(source_ids=['S_SINGLETON_READ','S_TRACKER','S_ACTIVATE','S_READ_REPLY','S_READ_API','S_REMOVAL_OPTION'],expectation_ids=['S_READ_SAFE_EXPECTATION','S_SINGLETON_EXPECTATION'],binding_ids=['BIND_SINGLETON_READ','BIND_SINGLETON_TEST'],derivation='S_READ_SAFE_EXPECTATION attributes safe read certification to communication with the quorum. S_SINGLETON_EXPECTATION describes the communication-free case specifically as a single voting member that is the leader. Taken together, that local self-certification is qualified by local identity, not merely a cardinality-one configuration. This is a derived local implementation responsibility, not a claim that all removed-node API calls are forbidden or every emitted ReadState directly completes a linearizable application read. A singleton configuration whose sole voter is another node provides no local quorum support to the responding instance. The implementation observation that the predicate omits identity motivates checking the relation but does not supply the normative expectation.',applicability='S_REMOVAL_OPTION documents optional removal step-down without stating that false disables ReadOnlySafe. RawNode.ReadIndex has no removal precondition and RawNode has no lifecycle Stop API; caller retirement remains an explicit excluded deployment policy. The actual history activates removal through committed entry application, without illegal ApplyConfChange injection. ReadState emission, not subsequent application read, is the selected endpoint.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['StepDownOnRemoval=true prevents this path by changing role; that is a valid protection and a separate control.','External caller retirement prevents reachability but does not change the conditional responsibility for this explicitly live instance.','The documented application-progress condition limits broader consequences and is not silently replaced by an assumed application read.']))\nbindings=[]\nfor i,mat,sym,a,z,desc in [('BIND_SINGLETON_READ','S_PROPOSE','stepLeader',1267,1364,'Leader ReadIndex singleton branch bypasses a quorum round.'),('BIND_SINGLETON_TEST','S_TRACKER','IsSingleton',160,162,'Predicate establishes singleton cardinality without local node identity.')]:\n bindings.append(dict(id=i,material_id=mat,symbol=sym,start_line=a,end_line=z,description=desc,pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claim['id'],source_ids=[mat,'S_SINGLETON_EXPECTATION','S_READ_SAFE_EXPECTATION'],rationale='Connects the documented self-certification expectation to '+desc)]))\ns=dict(action='obligation',rationale='Register the observed cardinality-versus-identity question with a narrow derived read-certification responsibility. Preserve application endpoint and caller-retirement limits instead of claiming a client consistency violation.',map_path='read-map.json',map_changes={'core_overview':dict(impact='dependency',source_ids=['S_SINGLETON_READ','S_ACTIVATE','S_REMOVAL_OPTION'],rationale='Add the concrete singleton self-certification connection to membership and role retention.',preserves='C_STALE_APPEND_COMPLETION and its producer/consumer map, scope, driver and observations are unchanged. New read/configuration facts do not challenge that reviewed bounded result.')},question=q,obligation=claim,bindings=bindings,sources=[dict(id='S_SINGLETON_READ',file='raft.go',start_line=1346,end_line=1364,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='S_SINGLETON_EXPECTATION',file='raft.go',start_line=1346,end_line=1348,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='S_READ_SAFE_EXPECTATION',file='raft.go',start_line=231,end_line=242,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='S_REMOVAL_OPTION',file='raft.go',start_line=280,end_line=285,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='S_MEMBERSHIP_DOC',file='doc.go',start_line=261,end_line=283,kind='document_statement')],feedback=dict(ref_ids=['6127b12776d14d5f8a2557f7ecda3ef7','S_READ_SAFE_EXPECTATION','S_SINGLETON_READ','S_REMOVAL_OPTION','S_MEMBERSHIP_DOC'],answered='The removal history completed in both option modes. Without step-down, node 1 retained StateLeader and voters=[2] after applying removal at index 4, then emitted ReadState index 4 after node 2 elected itself and applied a new value at index 6. With step-down, node 1 was leaderless follower and emitted no ReadState. Source inspection distinguishes this cardinality-only shortcut from the normal read acknowledgement path. The two-node configuration is discouraged for availability, not prohibited by S_MEMBERSHIP_DOC; neither participant fails in this history.',remaining=['Execute a formal emitted-result implies local-sole-voter check with independently observed configuration and per-request completion.','Retain the permitted no-response control without requiring eventual success.','No application-served stale read or broader linearizability consequence has been observed.'],understanding='updated',rationale='The next discriminator is a narrow eligibility implication at ReadState emission, not a stronger equality or guaranteed read completion. This captures the source-supported local responsibility and is directly executable using the explored history. Storage overwrite extensions and the synchronous ordering discrepancy remain independent frontier options.'))\nPath('submission-read-obligation.json').write_text(json.dumps(s,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\npython3 make_read_obligation.py\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));p=subprocess.run(r['validation']['command']+['submission-read-obligation.json'],capture_output=True,text=True);print(p.stdout);print(p.stderr)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
